          "question": "Bacteria increase from 5 x 10^3 to 1.3 x 10^5 cells per cm3 in 4 hours. Calculate the growth rate constant k.",
          "status": "ready",
          "answer": "k = 0.81 per hour (h^-1).",
          "steps": [
            "Exponential growth follows N = N0 e^(kt), so k = ln(N/N0) / t.",
            "N/N0 = (1.3 x 10^5) / (5 x 10^3) = 26.",
            "k = ln 26 / 4 = 3.258 / 4 = 0.81 per hour.",
            "The units are per hour (h^-1)."
          ]
