          "question": "Describe how the resting potential of -70 mV is maintained in the axon when no pressure is applied.",
          "status": "ready",
          "answer": "The Na+/K+ pump actively moves 3 Na+ out and 2 K+ in using ATP, and the membrane is more permeable to K+, giving a negative inside.",
